  'Sensi ferini': {
    base: '*Your senses reach beyond sight.*',
    '2014': "You do not suffer **disadvantage** on attack rolls against creatures you cannot see (unless you are blinded or deafened) and you sense the location of any **invisible** creature within **9 m**, as long as it is not hidden and you are not blinded or deafened.",
    '2024': "You gain **Blindsight with a range of 9 m**: within that distance you perceive your surroundings without needing to see.",
  },
  'Andatura nel terreno': 'Natural difficult terrain does not slow you down.',
  'Nascondersi in piena vista': 'You can hide by staying still and camouflaged.',
  'Svanire': 'As a bonus action you can Hide; you cannot be tracked.',
  'Sterminatore di nemici': {
    base: "*The hunter's finishing blow.*",
    '2014': "Once per turn you can add your **Wisdom** modifier to the attack roll **or** the damage roll of an attack against your **favoured enemy**.",
    '2024': "The extra damage die of **Hunter's Mark** becomes a **d10** instead of a d6.",
  },
  'Stregoneria innata': "Magic flows naturally in your veins, the gift of a bloodline, an otherworldly influence or a cosmic quirk. You choose a Sorcerous Origin (e.g. Draconic, Wild Magic, Aberrant, Clockwork) that shapes your unique powers from 1st level and grants extra features at 3rd, 6th, 14th and 18th level.",
  'Origine stregonesca': 'You choose the source of your innate magic, such as a Draconic Bloodline or Wild Magic. That choice grants you specific features at 1st, 6th, 14th and 18th level.',
  'Fonte di magia': 'You draw on an inner well of magical energy represented by **Sorcery Points** (equal to your sorcerer level).\n\n- **Creating slots:** as a bonus action you can spend Sorcery Points to create spell slots (1st = 2 pts, 2nd = 3 pts, 3rd = 5 pts, 4th = 6 pts, 5th = 7 pts).\n- **Converting slots:** as a bonus action you can sacrifice a spell slot to gain Sorcery Points equal to the slot level.\n- Sorcery Points can never exceed your maximum, and they recharge at the end of a long rest.',
  'Metamagia': "Your intuitive grasp of spells lets you reshape them to suit your needs.\n\n- You learn **2 Metamagic options** of your choice (two more at 10th and one more at 17th level).\n- When you cast a spell, you spend Sorcery Points to apply a Metamagic option (only one option per spell, except for *Empowered* and *Careful*).",
  'Recupero stregonesco': 'When you finish a short rest, you can regain a number of spent Sorcery Points equal to half your sorcerer level (rounded down). You can use this feature once per long rest.',
  'Ristoro stregonesco': 'At 20th level, you regain 4 spent Sorcery Points every time you finish a short rest.',
  'Stregoneria incarnata': 'When you use your Innate Sorcery, you can spend 2 Sorcery Points to empower it for 1 minute, gaining your subclass’s specific benefits (e.g. flight, extra defences or auras of chaos) and the ability to cast 2 spells per turn (one as an action and one as a bonus action, if their casting times allow it).',
  'Apoteosi arcana': 'You have become a living fusion with arcane magic. Once per turn, when you apply a Metamagic option to a spell, that option’s Sorcery Point cost is reduced by 2 (minimum 0, making 1- and 2-point options entirely free).',
  'Magia del patto': 'A few spell slots (1-4) always at their highest level, which you regain on every short or long rest.',
